{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213421,"nonce":"7jpYukrEHlmEtMpRTjHM26+nxAA=","title":"caribou_abi: layouts, Value tags, allocation kinds, descriptor table, handshake","message":"The zero-dependency crate every plugin and runtime compiles against. It never\ndefines a symbol of its own; it only describes what the core exports and what\ncrosses the boundary.\n\nContents: HashLink layouts spelled as hl.h spells them (hl_type and its detail\nstructs, vdynamic, vobj, varray, vclosure, vvirtual, vdynobj, venum, vstring,\nhl_runtime_obj); the TypeDesc prefix rule (word zero of every object is a\ndescriptor whose first 32 bytes are an hl_type); the core Value NaN-box tag\nlayout; allocation kinds with HashLink's MEM_KIND numbering; the plugin\ndescriptor table (class, method, static flag, typed signature with per-param\ntags and dynamic/variadic/effectful flags, function pointer) merged from\nrayzor-plugin and ZRTL; the version handshake symbol; error kinds.\n\nSources merged: wlift_abi (opaque VM, slot API, allocator interposition,\nversion handshake), rayzor-plugin (structured descriptor table, two link\nstrategies), ZRTL (typed signatures, static twin), hl_abi (HashLink layouts,\nDEFINE_PRIM resolver). ZRTL retires into this crate.\n\nLayout assertions are tests: sizes and offsets checked against hl.h's numbers.","files":null}]}